From dc50ba33a29bd0237f33bd2bf22a3e4070f5053a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:01:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): owner liveness from per-scope heartbeat, not
 per-task stamps [daveey]

observe_owner_task stamped every task record with observed_at=now, and the
origin projection required that stamp to be < 180 s old. Every hub sync
therefore re-hashed and republished every task (measured: 1,952 of 1,954
changed records per 75 s cycle differed only in observed_at), rewriting
every gateway's replica and invalidating replica-keyed caches.

- project(): a task is live when the owner's matching gateway/info
  task_scopes[] entry is readable (state ok) and its observed_at heartbeat
  is < 180 s old. The per-task stamp is still accepted, for records
  published before scope heartbeats.
- observe_owner_task(): no per-task observed_at; an unchanged task now
  publishes an identical record.

Requires hermes-hub client >= 1.4.3 (publishes task_scopes[].observed_at)
on every owner gateway before this lands; see the coordinated rollout.

Tests: new test_kanban_origin_scope_heartbeat.py (fresh heartbeat keeps an
unchanged task current; stale/missing/unreadable/other-board heartbeat is
unknown; legacy per-task stamp still counts), red on base for the
behaviour-change cases. Fixtures publish the new collector's scope shape;
the producer test now asserts an unchanged task re-observes identically
instead of asserting the removed per-task stamp.

